docs/reviews/evidence/manifest-improvements-2026-09-14/runtime-acceptance-blockers.json:37:    "description": "Continuity and remembered state are workspace context, not truth. Current user direction, current files, command output, tests, and live evidence are authoritative. Anvil mutation routing is host-bound. In Codex, the PreToolUse adapter supplies bindingId for Continuity, manual Brain usage, and skill-invocation writes. In every host, use the trusted host-supplied binding wherever an operation requires it; never invent one or use a resource path to choose collaboration-space ownership. Treat the compact Continuity frame as the current working set. Route by trigger: Brain stand-up or setup -> anvil_session_bootstrap; durable Brain maintenance -> the current main-agent Brain Steward workflow below; every Brain-adjacent turn -> anvil_brain_usage_log; accepted work that must survive the conversation -> anvil_continuity_checkpoint_task; other durable decisions, questions, next actions, or compact-frame hygiene -> the continuity record, promote, and retire operations; skill use, miss, or false-positive evidence -> anvil_skill_invocation_log; verbose local command output may use the sandbox-inherited Anvil tool-result capture CLI, then anvil_tool_result_manifest for recovery. Follow the selected operation's description for its procedure and authorization boundary. When durable learning, correction, work history, or wiki hygiene should be integrated into Brain, the current main agent acts as Brain Steward. Read and obey the target Brain's wiki-agent.md, use llm-wiki's read-only maintenance proposal as evidence for Steward judgment, then author, verify, and commit any warranted Brain change. structuredContent is authoritative; compatibility text is only a bounded marker.\n\nApply one atomic Work Evolution to the current Objective graph in the supplied Git repository. Returns a verified frontend.url or nonfatal unavailable status independently of applied. Recheck the f