docs/reviews/evidence/manifest-improvements-2026-09-14/legacy-parent-dependencies.json:260:        "details": "Updated from Vik's 10 September 2026 correction. The instruction correction was completed in 2d6c0f8. Review the existing paired baseline display, stagnation, contributing-trade and concentration evidence with Vik. Identify what is missing from a proper naive-strategy view before choosing filters, entries or management changes. Validation data can be obtained when needed; acquiring or reserving it is not a completion gate for this task. Agree selection/validation boundaries when that work becomes relevant, before using new evidence to qualify a strategy. The current records retain original 2016–2022 history and do not establish a new validation split or strategy qualification.\n\nFEATURES & REPRESENTATIONS REVIEW — 10 September 2026. Requested by Vik as prioritization for this Tokyo Fix Objective. Read the five direct idea pages and the nested native adverse-first study under https://app.notion.com/p/3caeaab09d6981669086c49b2cdf64ff. Their old execution-order/status instructions are historical inputs; current graph and user direction govern. Notion was read only.\n\nStatus: Recommendation for Vik's review; not an accepted research contract or implementation launch.\n\nRecommended next question: How do naive Tokyo Fix winners and losers develop through the trade, and which differences become observable early enough to improve the remaining decision?\n\n1. Trade-path and excursion inspection, including adverse-first reversal. Complete the view of the actual naive trade: individual and distributional paths, favourable/adverse excursion magnitudes and timing, winner/loser trajectories, and relation to known stagnant intervals. This can distinguish early losses, reversals, late profit giveback and persistent losing paths without inventing a filter. Whole-trade path order is retrospective, not a live input. Source: https://app.notion.com/p/3ceeaab09d6981c99078fa13db9911a7\n\n2. Early path fingerprint versus remaining opportunity. Reuse raw early-path channels to ask whether observations already available change the value of continuing the original trade. Agree checkpoint, observation completeness, remaining target and marginal execution/cost treatment before implementation. Source: https://app.notion.com/p/3caeaab09d69819d8fc9d120291d33e1\n\n3. Information gain with feature-group ablation. After defining the causal decision, compare simple calendar, displacement and volatility baselines with raw path/activity/spread. Measure date-ordered held-out log-loss improvement/calibration and incremental group value; translate predictive improvement separately into net strategy value. Apply feature-subset ideas here rather than launching a separate search programme. Source: https://app.notion.com/p/3d2eaab09d69818b9a21e6f3b86adc08\n\n4. Roughness. A later candidate if observed paths suggest persistence/choppiness matters beyond return, trend and volatility. The page's Hurst/fractal proposals are untested choices, not required first implementations. Source: https://app.notion.com/p/3cbeaab09d6981b9a1e3f59f176e7380\n\n5. Fourier/STFT. Later still: test incremental value over raw path on the same causal observations; no reason yet to introduce specialised neural spectral models. Source: https://app.notion.com/p/3cbeaab09d69811d97e8c49d7ea387b6\n\nFeature-subset source: https://app.notion.com/p/3cbeaab09d6981e18ceece5978b2c29a\n\nVerified implementation inventory at repository 2d6c0f8: session heatmaps, PCA/Ward families and simple path/context/cost/cohort inspection exist. The current family window is 09:30–10:29; the agreed full-morning 09:00–11:29 study is not implemented. Midpoint short-side MFE/MAE and order summaries exist inside family_characterisation (manifold.py:1700–1752; definitions 1828–1847), not the requested native cTrader path audit. ctrader_reconcile.py normalizes trade execution/accounting fields; neither original 90m report history nor create/close events includes native MFE/MAE paths or extreme timestamps.\n\nRaw four-channel 09:56–10:10 fingerprint arrays exist (manifold.py:1867–1981). Their displayed winsorisation and standardisation fit across the selected sample; later predictive use must fit transformations in training folds. Outcomes (manifold.py:3178–3308) starts at 10:30 and ends 11:29 or 14:59; winner/loser labels are upper/lower quartiles of upward midpoint change, not net profitability of the 09:55–11:25 short. model_gate is explicitly descriptive_only/unfitted. Reuse the raw representation while agreeing a strategy-aligned decision and target, rather than reusing these labels.\n\nImplementation not established for the proposed information/surprise scan, feature-subset ablation, roughness or Fourier/STFT in the inspected manifold.py, ctrader_reconcile.py, web/app.js and tests. This is a bounded source audit, not proof of absence outside this checkout or new empirical test results.\n\nAccepted 2016–2022 original cTrader ledger differs from the dashboard's reconstructed 2017–2020 quotes and strategy proxy. The CSV contains fills/costs/outcomes but no MFE/MAE path or timestamps. A compatible intratrade source and explicit join/coverage/price contract is necessary for a path study; acquiring or reserving future validation data remains deferred until relevant. Source definitions: TOKYO_FIX_BASELINE_INVENTORY.md; DATA_RECONSTRUCTION.md; artifacts/tokyo-fix-baselines-20260909/README.md and all-weekdays.csv.\n\nFull-morning family taxonomy and further clustering, recurrence or neural representations are not prerequisites to the recommended direct trade-path question. Reprioritising any deferred study needs an explicit graph decision; this assessment does not resume it.\n\nNo checkpoint, new study window, cohort definition, price/cost boundary, target, feature set, success tolerance or validation split has been selected by this review. Vik explicitly accepted this review as complete on 10 September 2026. The recorded recommendation remains the source for later research-contract shaping. Recommended first move is the direct baseline path/excursion audit; any later prediction study is separate from proving an economically useful trading policy.\n\nCOMPLETION — 10 September 2026: Vik confirmed that recording the review in this Task is sufficient and explicitly directed that it be marked complete. He identified dashboard alignment to the intended 90-minute trade as follow-up work. This closes the review and prioritization task; it does not claim the path audit, information scan or later feature experiments have run.",
docs/reviews/evidence/manifest-improvements-2026-09-14/legacy-parent-dependencies.json:366:      "details": "CURRENT RESULTS — W1.5.1–W1.5.5 are resolved under the agreed studies and candidate decisions. W1.5.3 directly shows current checkpoint position associated with original wins (ahead68.5%,behind38.0%). W1.5.2 fitted models found current position supplies the strongest contribution. W1.5.4's187exact-pair rebound contrast had99vs97wins and−A$1.37mean paired net difference, giving no generally favourable rebound rule.\n\nW1.5.5.1's explicitly authorized simple choppiness model comparison is complete: Controls494correct versus added493of776, primary−0.004987bits95%[−0.011940,+0.001783], no supported extra gain; park this measure for the tested model. W1.5.5.2 spectral candidate parked as agreed. Full evidence artifacts/tokyo-fix-baselines-20260909/ROUGHNESS_FINDINGS.md; earlier reports retain their distinct questions and results.\n\nThese results do not prove all early-path information absent or establish an improved management rule. All inspected development, original fills/outcomes retained. No new data, threshold search or qualification. Further modelling and dashboard work remain paused beyond the completed specifically authorized roughness test. Choose the next research question deliberately with Vik.\n\nFOLLOW-UP COMPLETED — The proposed full-set pre-entry question was subsequently agreed and completed under W1.6 (task_07e9bbefdb92660a8cddca1506d6649e), method 5a5788d and findings df489fb. Its current results and full 1,816-trade coverage belong there. W1.5 remains complete at its historical study scopes; it does not establish a sizing or exit policy.",
