test/fixtures/manifest-rings-view.json:414:            "acceptance": "Selection, detail, arbitrary-depth expansion, pan, zoom, and live view continuity remain the existing product.",
test/fixtures/manifest-rings-view.json:700:              "details": "ID: M.1.1.2\nCross-cuts: M.1.1.1, M.2.1, M.2.7\nStatus: Accepted\nShaping focus: Addressed\nLevel 4 status: M.1.1.2.1–M.1.1.2.4 Accepted\nDecomposition review: Complete — all four Level 4 concepts addressed\nDecomposition: Complete\n\nLets Vik move through work while retaining orientation, context, and a clear route back.\n\nDECOMPOSITION — ACCEPTED\nWork navigation\n  ├─ Work finding — ADDRESSED\n  │    locate and open exact work\n  ├─ Graph navigation — ADDRESSED\n  │    current map UX and code validated\n  ├─ History navigation — ADDRESSED\n  │    inspect versions and return to now\n  └─ Navigation continuity — ADDRESSED\n       existing map invariant, not new build scope\n\nNavigation continuity records working map behaviour and constrains later navigation; it does not create another feature or subsystem.",
test/fixtures/manifest-rings-view.json:711:                  "details": "ID: M.1.1.2.1\nCross-cuts: M.1.1.1, M.2.7.1\nStatus: Accepted\nShaping focus: Addressed\nDecomposition: Complete; natural endpoint\n\nSearch and jump to an exact Objective, Workstream, or Task.\n\nBEHAVIOUR — ACCEPTED\n• Exact identity or direct reference opens exact work.\n• Name or text search returns bounded candidates with type and canonical lineage.\n• Zero candidates is Not found; several plausible candidates remain Ambiguous; Manifest never silently chooses.\n• Search names one current version and shows active filters, bounds, omissions, and continuation.\n• Completed and discontinued work stays findable; historical-only results remain clearly historical.\n• Selecting expands, centres, and opens the item but changes only Vik's view—never Current, Next, execution selection, or Work System state.\n• Navigation continuity preserves the prior position and route back.\n\nENDPOINT\nDirect lookup, bounded search, disambiguation, and opening are one locating operation, not child concepts.\n\nCURRENT IMPLEMENTATION MEANING\nThe retained capability is implemented through the reduced Git-backed Objective graph. Retired lifecycle, versioning, proposal, and governance mechanisms in the accepted-definition text above are historical only; the Delivery Invariant and Recovery Review govern the current meaning.",
test/fixtures/manifest-rings-view.json:781:                  "details": "ID: M.1.1.2.2\nCross-cuts: M.1.1.1.1, M.2.1, M.2.7\nStatus: Accepted\nShaping focus: Addressed\nDecomposition: Complete; natural endpoint\n\nThe current Manifest map is the validated Human-interface and implementation baseline.\n\nBEHAVIOUR — ACCEPTED\n• Click work for detail, expand and collapse branches, pan and zoom, and follow visible structure and relationships.\n• Revealing connected work preserves lineage or relationship meaning and centres the destination.\n• Relationship type and direction remain clear; the origin stays visible or has a route back through Navigation continuity.\n• Hidden branches and bounded results remain explicit.\n• One current agreed-state version supplies the view; live updates never mix versions.\n• Navigation changes only Vik's view and never any Work System fact.\n\nBUILD CONSTRAINT — ACCEPTED\nReuse the existing graph code as Manifest V2's implementation baseline. Refactor or replace only for a concrete integration, scale, accessibility, or testing need—never merely for architectural neatness.\n\nENDPOINT\nThe working current implementation already validates this one graph-traversal behaviour; no children are needed.\n\nCURRENT IMPLEMENTATION MEANING\nThe retained capability is implemented through the reduced Git-backed Objective graph. Retired lifecycle, versioning, proposal, and governance mechanisms in the accepted-definition text above are historical only; the Delivery Invariant and Recovery Review govern the current meaning.",
test/fixtures/manifest-rings-view.json:827:                  "title": "Navigation continuity",
test/fixtures/manifest-rings-view.json:829:                  "details": "ID: M.1.1.2.4\nCross-cuts: M.1.1.2.1, M.1.1.2.2, M.1.1.2.3\nStatus: Accepted\nShaping focus: Addressed\nDecomposition: Complete; natural endpoint\n\nPreserves Vik's current map position across valid live graph updates.\n\nBEHAVIOUR — ACCEPTED\n• The current map already preserves valid selection, expanded branches, viewport and zoom, and detail mode while valid updated graph data loads.\n• That working implementation is the baseline and should be reused.\n• Finding, graph, and history navigation must preserve the valid visual context they start from; continuity unique to one feature belongs to that feature when built.\n• View continuity is Human-interface behaviour only and never changes Work System state.\n\nENDPOINT\nThis creates no separate subsystem or additional build scope. It records an existing map invariant and a constraint on later navigation.\n\nCURRENT IMPLEMENTATION MEANING\nThe retained capability is implemented through the reduced Git-backed Objective graph. Retired lifecycle, versioning, proposal, and governance mechanisms in the accepted-definition text above are historical only; the Delivery Invariant and Recovery Review govern the current meaning.",
