docs/manifest-rings/manifest-ring.html:869:{"id":"agent-continuation","label":"Agent continuation","state":"primary","sublabel":"M.1.2.1.3 · Level 4 · Accepted · Both Level 5 concepts addressed · Decomposition complete.","body":"ID: M.1.2.1.3\nCross-cuts: M.1.2.1.1, M.1.2.1.2, M.2.5\nStatus: Accepted\nLevel 5 status: M.1.2.1.3.1–M.1.2.1.3.2 Accepted\nDecomposition review: Complete — both Level 5 concepts addressed\nDecomposition: Complete\n\nThe durable preservation and later safe restoration of an active or waiting agent position without treating session continuity as canonical work state.\n\nDECOMPOSITION — ACCEPTED\n\nAgent continuation\n  ├─ Continuation checkpoint — ADDRESSED\n  │    durable agent position and unfinished intent\n  └─ Restoration reconciliation — ADDRESSED\n       compare checkpoint with current authoritative graph\n\nCheckpoint capture and later reconciliation have different triggers. The graph remains authoritative for work; continuation records only where this agent stopped and what it intended to do next.","kind":"decomposed"},
docs/manifest-rings/manifest-ring.html:877:{"id":"work-navigation","label":"Work navigation","state":"primary","sublabel":"M.1.1.2 · Level 3 · Accepted · All four Level 4 concepts addressed · Decomposition complete.","body":"ID: M.1.1.2\nCross-cuts: M.1.1.1, M.2.1, M.2.7\nStatus: Accepted\nShaping focus: Addressed\nLevel 4 status: M.1.1.2.1–M.1.1.2.4 Accepted\nDecomposition review: Complete — all four Level 4 concepts addressed\nDecomposition: Complete\n\nLets Vik move through work while retaining orientation, context, and a clear route back.\n\nDECOMPOSITION — ACCEPTED\nWork navigation\n  ├─ Work finding — ADDRESSED\n  │    locate and open exact work\n  ├─ Graph navigation — ADDRESSED\n  │    current map UX and code validated\n  ├─ History navigation — ADDRESSED\n  │    inspect versions and return to now\n  └─ Navigation continuity — ADDRESSED\n       existing map invariant, not new build scope\n\nNavigation continuity records working map behaviour and constrains later navigation; it does not create another feature or subsystem.","kind":"decomposed"},
docs/manifest-rings/manifest-ring.html:878:{"id":"work-finding","label":"Work finding","state":"primary","sublabel":"M.1.1.2.1 · Level 4 · Accepted · Review addressed · Natural endpoint.","body":"ID: M.1.1.2.1\nCross-cuts: M.1.1.1, M.2.7.1\nStatus: Accepted\nShaping focus: Addressed\nDecomposition: Complete; natural endpoint\n\nSearch and jump to an exact Objective, Workstream, or Task.\n\nBEHAVIOUR — ACCEPTED\n• Exact identity or direct reference opens exact work.\n• Name or text search returns bounded candidates with type and canonical lineage.\n• Zero candidates is Not found; several plausible candidates remain Ambiguous; Manifest never silently chooses.\n• Search names one current version and shows active filters, bounds, omissions, and continuation.\n• Completed and discontinued work stays findable; historical-only results remain clearly historical.\n• Selecting expands, centres, and opens the item but changes only Vik's view—never Current, Next, execution selection, or Work System state.\n• Navigation continuity preserves the prior position and route back.\n\nENDPOINT\nDirect lookup, bounded search, disambiguation, and opening are one locating operation, not child concepts.","kind":"decomposed"},
docs/manifest-rings/manifest-ring.html:879:{"id":"graph-navigation","label":"Graph navigation","state":"primary","sublabel":"M.1.1.2.2 · Level 4 · Accepted · Current UX and code validated · Natural endpoint.","body":"ID: M.1.1.2.2\nCross-cuts: M.1.1.1.1, M.2.1, M.2.7\nStatus: Accepted\nShaping focus: Addressed\nDecomposition: Complete; natural endpoint\n\nThe current Manifest map is the validated Human-interface and implementation baseline.\n\nBEHAVIOUR — ACCEPTED\n• Click work for detail, expand and collapse branches, pan and zoom, and follow visible structure and relationships.\n• Revealing connected work preserves lineage or relationship meaning and centres the destination.\n• Relationship type and direction remain clear; the origin stays visible or has a route back through Navigation continuity.\n• Hidden branches and bounded results remain explicit.\n• One current agreed-state version supplies the view; live updates never mix versions.\n• Navigation changes only Vik's view and never any Work System fact.\n\nBUILD CONSTRAINT — ACCEPTED\nReuse the existing graph code as Manifest V2's implementation baseline. Refactor or replace only for a concrete integration, scale, accessibility, or testing need—never merely for architectural neatness.\n\nENDPOINT\nThe working current implementation already validates this one graph-traversal behaviour; no children are needed.","kind":"decomposed"},
docs/manifest-rings/manifest-ring.html:881:{"id":"navigation-continuity","label":"Navigation continuity","state":"primary","sublabel":"M.1.1.2.4 · Level 4 · Accepted · Existing behaviour satisfies scope · Natural endpoint.","body":"ID: M.1.1.2.4\nCross-cuts: M.1.1.2.1, M.1.1.2.2, M.1.1.2.3\nStatus: Accepted\nShaping focus: Addressed\nDecomposition: Complete; natural endpoint\n\nPreserves Vik's current map position across valid live graph updates.\n\nBEHAVIOUR — ACCEPTED\n• The current map already preserves valid selection, expanded branches, viewport and zoom, and detail mode while valid updated graph data loads.\n• That working implementation is the baseline and should be reused.\n• Finding, graph, and history navigation must preserve the valid visual context they start from; continuity unique to one feature belongs to that feature when built.\n• View continuity is Human-interface behaviour only and never changes Work System state.\n\nENDPOINT\nThis creates no separate subsystem or additional build scope. It records an existing map invariant and a constraint on later navigation.","kind":"decomposed"},
docs/manifest-rings/manifest-ring.html:887:{"id":"durable-work-continuity","label":"Durable work continuity","state":"primary","sublabel":"M.2.5 · Level 2 · Accepted · Decomposition complete — Durable work state addressed.","body":"ID: M.2.5\nCross-cuts: None identified\nLevel 3 status: Accepted.\nDecomposition review: Complete — Durable work state addressed.\nDecomposition: Complete.\n\nManifest preserves durable work state so Objectives, Workstreams, and Tasks can continue without reconstruction.","kind":"decomposed"},
docs/manifest-rings/manifest-ring.html:924:{"id":"stable-work-identity","label":"Stable work identity","state":"primary","sublabel":"M.2.7.1 · Level 3 · Accepted · Review addressed · Natural endpoint.","body":"ID: M.2.7.1\nStatus: Accepted\nCross-cuts: M.2.2.1, M.2.5.1, M.2.5.1.4.3.3, M.2.6.1, M.2.6.2, M.2.6.3, M.2.6.5, M.2.7.2, M.2.7.3.2\nReview pass: Addressed\nDecomposition: Complete; natural endpoint.\n\nEvery Objective, Workstream, and Task retains one permanent identity as it evolves.\n\nBEHAVIOUR — ACCEPTED\n\nAccepted creation of Work W\n          ↓ assign atomically\nOne permanent identity I\n          ↓ remains I through\nrevision · movement · focus · interruption · return · completion · discontinuation · restoration · divergent candidates\n\nDistinct work from W → new identity + provenance\nSame-work reconciliation → retain I\nDistinct-source convergence → new identity linked to every source\n\n• Creation assigns exactly one identity; failure exposes none and retry is idempotent.\n• Identity is immutable, never reassigned, and never reused after any ending.\n• Name, content, parent, position, ordering, focus, availability, version, and lifecycle state do not define identity.\n• Equal names, content, or positions never establish identity by inference.\n• Every version and lifecycle record refers to the identity it concerns.\n• Copies, split results, branches, materially different outcomes, and other distinct work receive new linked identities.\n• One identity never becomes several; several existing identities never collapse into one.\n• Convergence creates a new identity while every source identity and history remains intact.\n• Completed and discontinued identities remain addressable; renewed intent creates new linked work.\n• Identity, work, lineage, and provenance validate and preserve atomically; collisions and stale claims fail or route through divergence handling.\n\nACCEPTED ANCHOR\nOrdinary changes and same-work reconciliation retain identity. Distinct work receives a new identity. Converging distinct identities creates one new identity linked to every preserved source.\n\nENDPOINT\nComplete here. Assignment, immutability, continuity, non-reuse, and transformation rules form one identity invariant; lineage and provenance are separate concepts.","kind":"decomposed"},
docs/manifest-rings/manifest-ring.html:934:{"id":"task-execution-readiness","label":"Task execution readiness","state":"primary","sublabel":"M.2.1.3.4 · Level 4 · Accepted · All four dimensions addressed · Decomposition complete.","body":"ID: M.2.1.3.4\nCross-cuts: M.1.2.1.2, M.1.2.3, M.2.4.1, M.2.6.1, M.2.6.2\nStatus: Accepted\nShaping focus: Addressed\nLevel 5 status: M.2.1.3.4.1–M.2.1.3.4.4 Accepted\nDecomposition review: Complete — all four Level 5 dimensions addressed\nDecomposition: Complete\n\nAn explainable account of whether a Task is sufficiently understood and supported to begin, what uncertainty remains, and what must resolve before blocking uncertainty is cleared.\n\nREADINESS MODEL — ACCEPTED\nEach dimension is Known, Accepted assumption, or Unresolved, with rationale and evidence. Every unresolved item says whether it blocks execution and what resolves it. Overall readiness is derived as Ready, Conditional, or Not ready. Material resolution work becomes its own research, prototype, or decision Task.","kind":"decomposed"},
