docs/plans/2026-06-22-anvil-mcp-brain-v0.md:618:Bootstrap should be a compact orientation and routing packet, not a full memory dump and not a second Continuity.
docs/plans/2026-06-22-anvil-mcp-brain-v0.md:628:Bootstrap should return enough status to start safely, then point the agent toward richer Continuity, Brain, or Loci calls as needed. It should not own durable facts or duplicate the active working frame. Continuity owns live working state, Brain owns durable synthesized memory, and Loci owns code navigation.
