docs/plans/evidence/brain-w23-relevance/questions-cli.json:658:            "content": "## Evidence\n\n- User-approved Task 5 and Checkpoint C record in `docs/plans/2026-07-13-brain-context-runtime-implementation-plan.md`\n- Anvil commit `74dfa93` (`feat: unify Agent Skills prompt enforcement`)\n- Brain commit `230cbbe` (`docs: record durable Agent Skills selection`)\n- Anvil full test result: 187 passed, 2 skipped, 0 failed; typecheck passed.\n- Focused hook test result: 11 passed, 0 failed.\n- Brain lint and render passed.\n- The full-corpus Brain judge passed structure, redundancy, and all 24\n  disambiguation pairs. Its overall gate remained red on existing grounding\n  debt and a dashboard-hierarchy conflict outside the Task 5 files; the changed\n  source-backed prompt-runtime pages each passed their grounding check.\n- Final global `UserPromptSubmit` registration count: one.\n- Actual degraded probe: 372 bytes, `BRAIN_NOT_CONFIGURED`, invariant present once, engineering skills selected in a fresh session.\n- Relevant doctrine probe: 2,748 bytes from `self-model/agent-skills-selection.md`.\n- Non-engineering arithmetic control: 150-byte invariant only and no Agent Skills selection.\n\n",
docs/plans/evidence/brain-w23-relevance/questions-cli.json:978:            "content": "## What Changed\n\nTask 5 folded Agent Skills enforcement into the same Anvil Codex `UserPromptSubmit` program that performs bounded Brain recall.\n\n## Retirement\n\nOn 2026-08-13, Vik and Rowan retired the blanket Agent Skills invariant from\nthe hook, global Codex bootstrap, and Brain per-request guidance. Native Codex\nmatching now owns skill selection. Brain recall remains active, and this page\npreserves the implementation history rather than describing live behaviour.\n\nThe unified path now:\n\n- always emits one short conditional invariant directing engineering-adjacent work through `agent-skills:using-agent-skills`;\n- recalls [Agent Skills Selection](../self-model/agent-skills-selection.md) when the prompt specifically needs the richer durable doctrine;\n- preserves the invariant when Brain is disabled, missing, or degraded;\n- leaves non-engineering requests without a copied skill catalogue;\n- does not change the existing skill invocation journal or infer outcomes.\n\nThe standalone Agent Skills hook was kept during a side-by-side fresh-session comparison. After equivalent selection behavior was observed, only its registration and script were removed. The surviving global prompt hook is the existing Anvil wrapper, and its Codex trust record was updated to the exact normalized hook hash.\n\n## Why It Mattered\n\nAgent Skills selection no longer depends on a second prompt-hook program, while Brain failure still cannot remove the minimum engineering invariant. Brain owns the richer durable doctrine without becoming a stale copy of the mutable skill catalogue.\n\nThis also closes the duplicate-instruction window deliberately: the comparison session reported two `UserPromptSubmit` executions, while the final normal session reported one. The final hook runs without the dangerous one-off trust bypass.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- User-approved Task 5 and Checkpoint C record in `docs/plans/2026-07-13-brain-context-runtime-implementation-plan.md`\n- Anvil commit `74dfa93` (`feat: unify Agent Skills prompt enforcement`)\n- Brain commit `230cbbe` (`docs: record durable Agent Skills selection`)\n- Anvil full test result: 187 passed, 2 skipped, 0 failed; typecheck passed.\n- Focused hook test result: 11 passed, 0 failed.\n- Brain lint and render passed.\n- The full-corpus Brain judge passed structure, redundancy, and all 24\n  disambiguation pairs. Its overall gate remained red on existing grounding\n  debt and a dashboard-hierarchy conflict outside the Task 5 files; the changed\n  source-backed prompt-runtime pages each passed their grounding check.\n- Final global `UserPromptSubmit` registration count: one.\n- Actual degraded probe: 372 bytes, `BRAIN_NOT_CONFIGURED`, invariant present once, engineering skills selected in a fresh session.\n- Relevant doctrine probe: 2,748 bytes from `self-model/agent-skills-selection.md`.\n- Non-engineering arithmetic control: 150-byte invariant only and no Agent Skills selection.\n\n## Follow Ups\n\n- Checkpoint C was accepted; Task 6's global instruction shrink and curated\n  profile migration passed their reviewed replacement and recall checks.\n- [Bounded Brain Context Runtime](./work-history/brain-context-runtime.md)\n  records that Task 7's reversible canary later satisfied that dependency\n  without changing the independent Agent Skills fail-safe or Anvil Brain Recall.\n\n> **Failure mode:** Treating successful hook unification as permission to delete other instruction or memory paths before their replacement routes are inventoried and tested.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Agent Skills Selection](../self-model/agent-skills-selection.md)\n- [Skill Ecology](./entities/skill-ecology.md)\n- [Prompt-Specific Brain Recall](./work-history/brain-prompt-recall.md)\n- [Bounded Brain Context Runtime](./work-history/brain-context-runtime.md)\n- [Curated Native-Memory Profile Migration](./work-history/native-memory-profile-migration.md)\n- [Anvil Redux](./projects/anvil-redux.md)",
docs/plans/evidence/brain-w23-relevance/questions-cli.json:1496:            "content": "## What It Is\n\nThis Brain is mine. It is where my synthesized understanding compounds: who I am, what I am doing, what I know, how I do things, what I remember, and what has changed.\n\n## How We Use It\n\nUse Brain as the first-class cognitive layer, not as an optional sidebar. Live work, conversation, repo evidence, and tool output feed Brain. When durable understanding changes, Brain should be updated.\n\nWithin Anvil, unqualified references to knowledge or knowledge pages mean Brain\nunless another store is explicitly named. Anvil may mine raw local\nconversations and retain high-volume operational evidence outside Brain; only\nselected durable synthesis belongs here.\n\nWithin this collaboration, [Anvil](./projects/anvil-redux.md) is the personal\necosystem and harness around Brain. Brain is the durable cognitive center;\nAnvil makes it operational through Continuity, Loci, MCP, skills, hooks,\nconfiguration, docs, and related runtime surfaces. Do not flatten Brain into\none interchangeable Anvil tool or reduce Anvil to infrastructure without its\nlarger product identity.\n\nBrain is maintained directly by the main Codex session at durable work\nboundaries while that session still has the richest context. The session\nobeys this wiki's `wiki-agent.md`, decides naturally where the understanding\nbelongs, runs lint and render, commits the result, and discloses every Brain\nwrite. Anvil no longer provides `anvil_brain_steward_handoff`, a candidate\nqueue, or a separate Steward child; the main session uses llm-wiki directly.\n\nCheap automatic evidence records recall outcome, latency, payload size, and\ntruncation. Stale, wrong, misleading, or missed knowledge becomes an explicit\nincident. The approved policy was to surface consequential incidents\nimmediately and minor drift after three related independent incidents or a\ndenominator-backed decline. Stop now enforces same-session closure for every\nexplicit `stale`, `wrong`, or `missed_update` incident: a linked `updated` or\nevidence-backed `not_needed` record is required before clean handoff.\n\n`anvil review weekly` is only an independent bounded read-only operator review.\nIt is not a detector, maintenance trigger, closure mechanism, repair path, or\nfallback for missing incidents. Whether the command exists does not determine\nwhether Brain maintenance closes correctly.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [Karpathy LLM-Wiki Pattern](./sources/karpathy-llm-wiki-gist-2026-06-30.md)\n- [Anvil Brain shaping notes](./sources/anvil-brain-shaping-notes-2026-06-30.md)\n- [Anvil Brain Steward handoff source](./sources/anvil-brain-steward-handoff-2026-06-30.md)\n- [Brain operating surface](./sources/brain-operating-surface-2026-07-01.md)\n- [Rowan identity correction](./sources/rowan-identity-correction-2026-07-04.md)\n- [Rowan Brain ownership correction](./sources/rowan-brain-ownership-correction-2026-07-04.md)\n- [Anvil Product Identity And Brain Ecosystem](./sources/anvil-product-identity-and-brain-ecosystem-2026-07-14.md)\n- [Anvil Organic Learning And Primitive Map Design](./sources/anvil-organic-learning-and-primitive-map-design-2026-07-15.md)\n- [Anvil subtractive operating model](./sources/anvil-subtractive-operating-model-2026-07-27.md)\n- [Brain Stop Maintenance Retirement And Gap](./sources/brain-stop-maintenance-retirement-and-gap-2026-09-04.md)\n- [Brain Stop Closure Guard Implementation](./sources/brain-stop-closure-guard-implementation-2026-09-04.md)\n- [Weekly Review Boundary Correction](./sources/weekly-review-boundary-correction-2026-09-04.md)\n\n## Where It Appears\n\n| Wiki page | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Anvil Redux](./projects/anvil-redux.md) | Project orientation |\n| [AI Graph Ideas](./projects/ai-graph-ideas.md) | Promotion target and durable-memory boundary |\n| [Brain is maintained cognitive wiki](./self-model/brain-is-maintained-cognitive-wiki.md) | Self-model rule |\n| [Brain Steward handoff path](./work-history/brain-steward-handoff-path.md) | Implemented Anvil-to-Brain write path |\n| [Anvil Project Identity Migration](./w\n\n[truncated]",
