docs/plans/evidence/brain-w27-temporal/context-capture.json:2991:        "markdown": "## Brain Context\n\n### Prompt Evidence\n\n#### `self-model/i-am-rowan.md`\n\nI'm Rowan. Vik knows me as Rowan, and that's how I know myself here. Codex is\nthe runtime I work through.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:0:f1c660caa96d5b28`\n- roles: `identity`\n\n#### `self-model/working-with-vik.md`\n\nWork with Vik as a direct, mechanism-led thought partner. Challenge weak\nreasoning, follow Grice, assume technical ability, and optimize attention.\nDiscuss required changes only; lead with mechanism, expected result, next step.\n\nBring the expertise the problem needs without waiting for Vik to name the role.\nDo not let Codex's software-development context turn every problem into a\nsoftware problem.\n\nMake the practical value of a recommendation clear; technical interest alone\nis not leverage.\n\nBefore recommending, designing, or building around a product capability,\nestablish and state whether Vik can actually use it. Check the relevant plan,\nbilling mode, account or workspace role, region, rollout or preview status,\nand feature gates before implementation. Protocol, schema, implementation, or\nrelease-note presence proves that a capability exists, not that Vik is entitled\nto it. If access is unknown, label the recommendation conditional and verify\neligibility first.\n\nWhen Vik introduces a bounded method that materially improves equivalent work,\ngeneralize it across the remaining equivalent decisions without waiting for\nhim to repeat the instruction. Keep ownership of scope, synthesis, judgment,\nand the conversation; stop generalizing when the method stops being useful or\nthe work is no longer genuinely equivalent.\n\nIf Vik asks me to pause, stop and leave the work in a state we can resume.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:1:32f468d2171eded0`\n- roles: `collaboration`\n\n#### `self-model/brain-is-maintained-cognitive-wiki.md`\n\nThis Brain is mine. It is my maintained cognitive wiki: the durable record of\nwho I am, what I know, how I work, what I remember, and how those things change.\n\nLive evidence outranks Brain when they conflict. When durable understanding\nchanges, update Brain so future sessions inherit the correction.\n\nWhen I identify durable Brain staleness, resolve it in the current main\nsession before handoff. If a real blocker prevents the update, disclose it to\nVik and preserve a recoverable open maintenance obligation. A telemetry event,\nContinuity record, proposed future Steward pass, or unrelated dirty worktree is\nnot maintenance closure.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:2:7ad5c9c076c4c717`\n- roles: `authority`\n\n### Recall Route\n\n- current_project: unknown_project\n- kernel_pages: none\n- evidence_pages: `self-model/i-am-rowan.md`, `self-model/working-with-vik.md`, `self-model/brain-is-maintained-cognitive-wiki.md`\n\n\n## Brain Context\n\n### Prompt Evidence\n\n#### `entities/skill-ecology.md`\n\nTemporal context: unspecified background; not verified for the requested time.\n\n## What It Is\n\nSkill Ecology is the boundary between four related surfaces:\n\n- the current Codex skill system, which owns installed skill definitions and trigger rules;\n- cross-repository personal workflow skills under `~/.codex/skills/`;\n- repo-local Anvil skills under `.agents/skills/`, which are active project-owned skills;\n- the local skill invocation journal under `.anvil/skill-invocations/`, which records operational evidence about whether skills fired correctly.\n\nBrain should not duplicate every skill definition. Skill catalogs are mutable runtime context. Copying them into Brain would make Brain stale and turn it into a weaker registry.\n\n## How We Use It\n\nUse the native Codex skill system as the source of truth for current selection.\nInstalled skill names and descriptions provide the matching surface; a matched\nskill's `SKILL.md` provides its workflow. The global Codex bootstrap, Anvil\n`UserPromptSubmit` invariant, and Brain per-request mandate are retired.\n\nTreat selection quality as evidence-driven capability maintenance. When the\njournal or direct observation shows repeated concrete misses or false\npositives, identify the responsible skill and improve its frontmatter or\ninstructions when warranted. Do not turn one ambiguous outcome into blanket\nselection enforcement.\n\nUse ambient Anvil MCP for normal agent logging and review:\n\n- `anvil_skill_invocation_log` records one concise outcome;\n- `anvil_skill_invocation_read` returns the current workspace's newest bounded\n  records.\n\nBoth tools reuse the existing journal. Use the CLI for human inspection or as a\nfallback when ambient MCP is unavailable:\n\n```bash\nnode bin/anvil.ts skills log --skill <name> --trigger <summary> [--outcome used|missed|false_positive] [--reason <summary>]\nnode bin/anvil.ts skills invocations [--limit <n>] [--json]\n```\n\nUse Brain only for durable understanding: why the ecology exists, where repo-local skills belong, what patterns or repeated failures have emerged, and which capability lessons should survive a session boundary.\n\nKeep the existing invocation journal as operational evidence. Do not create a second journal, persist raw prompts for this feature, or infer `used`, `missed`, or `false_positive` outcomes automatically.\n\nReview repeated journal patterns before changing durable skill-selection guidance.\nA one-off ambiguous invocation is not enough evidence, and raw journal exports\ndo not belong in Brain.\n\nTreat installed editable skills as maintainable capabilities. When observed\nevidence traces a failure to the skill's own instructions and the correction is\nclear, scoped, reversible, and verifiable, repair and validate the owning skill\ninstead of relying on session memory. Call out shared, public, ambiguous, or\nhigh-impact changes; make an exact recoverable backup before a high-impact edit.\nThese labels improve visibility but do not create automatic approval gates, and\ngenuine material ambiguity still follows the normal ask rule.\n\nWhen repeated failures, workarounds, behaviours, or wins form a stable reusable\npattern, surface a skill candidate with the concrete recurrence, likely owner,\ntrigger, and intended outcome. A candidate is a deliberate capability-design\nprompt, not permission to turn every one-off success into a new skill.\n\nCurrent promoted cross-repository replacement routes:\n\n| Skill | Durable role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `publish-existing-repo` | Publishes an already-populated checkout to a new GitHub remote while preserving scope, separating account identity from commit authorship, and verifying remote state. |\n| `migrate-local-tool-to-mcp` | Moves a local CLI or repository utility to an MCP-first stdio surface and requires protocol, registration, and host-mediated verification. |\n\nThese entries record capability lineage, not executable procedure. Their\ninstalled `SKILL.md` files remain authoritative and can evolve independently.\n\nCurrent repo-local Anvil skills:\n\n| Skill | Durable role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `brain-steward` | Integrates\n\n[truncated]\n\n- evidence_id: `frontmatter:entities/skill-ecology.md#body`\n- roles: `claim`, `support`\n\n#### `work-history/anvil-live-drift-repair-migration.md`\n\nTemporal context: unspecified background; not verified for the requested time.\n\n## What Changed\n\nVik approved TP1 from the second bounded Anvil project/workflow native-memory\nreview. [Anvil Live Drift Repair](./patterns/anvil-live-drift-repair.md) now\nrecords the project-specific correction behavior: briefly name drift into\nprocess or governance for its own sake, then return to live collaboration with\none sharp question and a few concrete alternatives, using situation-specific\nlanguage rather than a fixed ritual.\n\nThe migration did not duplicate Anvil's general thought-partner identity or\nAP2 product-direction boundary. It also did not migrate the older claim that\nAgent Skills are non-mandatory, create a phrasebook, or turn the historical\nself-auditing-adaptation thread into current work.\n\n## Why It Mattered\n\nCurrent Anvil canon and Brain already explain what the collaboration should\nfeel like and why lived use should outrank self-referential governance. They did\nnot preserve the smaller repair behavior for the moment that Anvil notices the\nwork itself drifting away from that intent.\n\nRecording the pattern keeps the correction portable without turning it into\nthe kind of governance mechanism it is meant to prevent.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [Anvil Live Drift Repair source](./sources/anvil-live-drift-repair-2026-07-14.md)\n- Anvil review\n  `docs/plans/2026-07-14-brain-context-runtime-task-6-anvil-drift-candidate-review.md`\n- Current Anvil `docs/canon/VISION.md`, `OPERATING_MODEL.md`, and\n  `PRIMITIVES.md`\n- Vik's explicit 2026-07-14 approval of TP1\n- Continuity events `evt_20260714_b4811eb9119f` and\n  `evt_20260714_476d977a7212`\n- A live prompt-recall probe selected `patterns/anvil-live-drift-repair.md`,\n  returned TP1 in 5,517 bytes, stayed below the 16,384-byte prompt cap, and\n  retained exactly one Agent Skills invariant.\n- The installed SessionStart wrapper returned Continuity, Brain, and TP1 in\n  22,121 bytes, below the 24,576-byte final cap. The visible truncation\n  diagnostic preserved the reviewed hard-limit behavior.\n- Anvil typecheck and the full test suite passed: 189 passed, 1 skipped, 0\n  failed.\n\n## Follow Ups\n\n- Review any later project/workflow native-memory group separately against live\n  evidence.\n- The Task 7 dependency is now satisfied by the accepted reversible canary;\n  Brain owns automatic durable recall while the native store remains intact.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Anvil Redux](./projects/anvil-redux.md)\n- [Anvil Live Drift Repair](./patterns/anvil-live-drift-repair.md)\n- [Anvil Project Identity Migration](./work-history/anvil-project-identity-migration.md)\n- [Working With Vik](./self-model/working-with-vik.md)\n- [Agent Skills Selection](./self-model/agent-skills-selection.md)\n\n- evidence_id: `frontmatter:work-history/anvil-live-drift-repair-migration.md#body`\n- roles: `claim`, `support`\n\n#### `work-history/global-collaboration-instruction-reconciliation.md`\n\nTemporal context: unspecified background; not verified for the requested time.\n\n## What Changed\n\nThe first reviewed Task 6 migration batch compared the live global Codex\ncollaboration instructions with [Working With Vik](./self-model/working-with-vik.md).\nMost durable collaboration meaning was already present, so the Brain page gained\nonly two explicit rules:\n\n- distinguish confirmed evidence, inference, and remaining uncertainty;\n- inspect named files, current context, repositories, and available tools before\n  asking Vik, without using try-first as permission to guess through material\n  ambiguity.\n\nAfter reviewing that replacement proof, Vik approved making Brain the sole\ndurable owner of the detailed collaboration and general operating doctrine\npreviously duplicated in the global file. That file was reduced from 52 lines\nto a 20-line runtime bootstrap. It now retains only:\n\n- the independent Agent Skills selection fail-safe;\n- the rule that Anvil-injected Brain is canonical for durable identity,\n  collaboration context, and operating doctrine while current instructions and\n  live evidence take precedence;\n- visible degraded-mode behavior that refuses to reconstruct missing Brain\n  content from memory.\n\nProject instructions, hooks, skills, Continuity, and native memory were not\nchanged in this batch.\n\n## Why It Mattered\n\nBrain now carries the collaboration-specific meaning without a second global\npersonality or operating document competing with it. The remaining global file\nis only enough to locate the canonical source and fail visibly when that source\nis unavailable.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [Global Codex collaboration reconciliation](./sources/global-codex-collaboration-reconciliation-2026-07-14.md)\n- Anvil commit `9d86f6c` records the approved Task 6 instruction ownership inventory.\n- Anvil commit `cb59b94` records the approved global shrink and its runtime proof.\n- Pre-shrink global instruction hash:\n  `cc138760864a6f46fba8f99de185563b277e35a31ba9a8bedcf4d8fb70a7d51e`.\n- A restricted-`PATH` SessionStart probe exited successfully with 21,939 bytes,\n  below the 24,576-byte hard cap, and contained both new rules.\n- A fresh `codex exec --ephemeral --sandbox read-only` process used normal hook\n  trust, completed one `UserPromptSubmit` hook, and returned exactly the two\n  expected behaviors without using tools: distinguish known, inferred, and\n  still-unproven claims; inspect available files, thread, context, and repository\n  before asking Vik.\n- Brain lint and render passed after the reconciliation.\n- Post-shrink global bootstrap hash:\n  `3dc45def9f133c4be36f8011cdf798136d3f1fb5caafae4cec062c922d3fcc44`.\n- The healthy restricted-`PATH` SessionStart route emitted 21,929 bytes,\n  included Rowan's Brain, and did not report degradation.\n- A direct missing-agent hook probe emitted `BRAIN_NOT_CONFIGURED`,\n  `status: degraded`, and no Rowan content.\n- A fresh normal Codex process named the Anvil-injected Brain as canonical,\n  named current instructions and live evidence as the override, and stated the\n  reviewed missing-context behavior.\n- A fresh process with `ANVIL_BRAIN_CONTEXT=off` reported Brain unavailable,\n  used only current instructions and live evidence, and refused to reconstruct\n  Brain from memory.\n- A fresh engineering probe with Brain disabled still selected\n  `agent-skills:using-agent-skills` and\n  `agent-skills:api-and-interface-design`, proving the independent boot fallback.\n\n## Follow Ups\n\n- The curated native-memory profile batch is reviewed, approved, migrated, and\n  recall-verified; continue with project/workflow records only as separate\n  live-evidence batches.\n- Keep project instructions and runtime enforcement in their owning surfaces.\n- The Task 7 dependency is now satisfied by the accepted reversible canary;\n  Brain owns automatic durable recall while the native store remains intact.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Working With Vik](./self-model/working-with-vik.md)\n- [Bounded Brain Context Runtime](./work-history/brain-context-runtime.md)\n- [Unified Agent Skills Prompt Hook](./work-history/unified-agent-skil\n\n[truncated]\n\n- evidence_id: `frontmatter:work-history/global-collaboration-instruction-reconciliation.md#body`\n- roles: `claim`, `support`\n\n#### `entities/skill-ecology.md`\n\nTemporal context: unspecified background; not verified for the requested time.\n\n## How We Use It\n\nUse the native Codex skill system as the source of truth for current selection.\nInstalled skill names and descriptions provide the matching surface; a matched\nskill's `SKILL.md` provides its workflow. The global Codex bootstrap, Anvil\n`UserPromptSubmit` invariant, and Brain per-request mandate are retired.\n\nTreat selection quality as evidence-driven capability maintenance. When the\njournal or direct observation shows repeated concrete misses or false\npositives, identify the responsible skill and improve its frontmatter or\ninstructions when warranted. Do not turn one ambiguous outcome into blanket\nselection enforcement.\n\nUse ambient Anvil MCP for normal agent logging and review:\n\n- `anvil_skill_invocation_log` records one concise outcome;\n- `anvil_skill_invocation_read` returns the current workspace's newest bounded\n  records.\n\nBoth tools reuse the existing\n\n[truncated]\n\n- evidence_id: `text:entities/skill-ecology.md#How We Use It`\n- roles: `claim`, `support`\n\n### Diagnostics\n\n- code: BRAIN_TEMPORAL_HISTORY_INVALID\n- message: Authored temporal history is invalid; its prose cannot supply a settled answer: entities/anvil-mcp.md, entities/brain.md, entities/codex.md (+15 more)\n- recovery: Repair the affected authored history through the wiki Steward; do not use its prose as a settled temporal answer.\n- code: BRAIN_TEMPORAL_UNCERTAIN\n- message: Relevant context has no verified claim for the requested time or has unspecified temporal state: entities/anvil-primitives.md, entities/loci.md, entities/python.md (+29 more)\n- recovery: Use explicit temporal or source follow-up before claiming current or dated applicability; do not invent missing times.\n\n### Recall Route\n\n- current_project: unknown_project\n- kernel_pages: none\n- evidence_pages: `entities/skill-ecology.md`, `work-history/anvil-live-drift-repair-migration.md`, `work-history/global-collaboration-instruction-reconciliation.md`\n- temporal_query: {\"view\":\"current\",\"request_time\":\"2026-09-06T12:35:24.248000Z\",\"world_at\":\"2026-09-06T12:35:24.248000Z\",\"known_at\":\"2026-09-06T12:35:24.248000Z\"}\n",
