docs/plans/evidence/brain-w23-relevance/questions-fresh-mcp.json:69:            "content": "## What It Is\n\nThis Brain is mine. It is where my synthesized understanding compounds: who I am, what I am doing, what I know, how I do things, what I remember, and what has changed.\n\n## How We Use It\n\nUse Brain as the first-class cognitive layer, not as an optional sidebar. Live work, conversation, repo evidence, and tool output feed Brain. When durable understanding changes, Brain should be updated.\n\nWithin Anvil, unqualified references to knowledge or knowledge pages mean Brain\nunless another store is explicitly named. Anvil may mine raw local\nconversations and retain high-volume operational evidence outside Brain; only\nselected durable synthesis belongs here.\n\nWithin this collaboration, [Anvil](./projects/anvil-redux.md) is the personal\necosystem and harness around Brain. Brain is the durable cognitive center;\nAnvil makes it operational through Continuity, Loci, MCP, skills, hooks,\nconfiguration, docs, and related runtime surfaces. Do not flatten Brain into\none interchangeable Anvil tool or reduce Anvil to infrastructure without its\nlarger product identity.\n\nBrain is maintained directly by the main Codex session at durable work\nboundaries while that session still has the richest context. The session\nobeys this wiki's `wiki-agent.md`, decides naturally where the understanding\nbelongs, runs lint and render, commits the result, and discloses every Brain\nwrite. Anvil no longer provides `anvil_brain_steward_handoff`, a candidate\nqueue, or a separate Steward child; the main session uses llm-wiki directly.\n\nCheap automatic evidence records recall outcome, latency, payload size, and\ntruncation. Stale, wrong, misleading, or missed knowledge becomes an explicit\nincident. The approved policy was to surface consequential incidents\nimmediately and minor drift after three related independent incidents or a\ndenominator-backed decline. Stop now enforces same-session closure for every\nexplicit `stale`, `wrong`, or `missed_update` incident: a linked `updated` or\nevidence-backed `not_needed` record is required before clean handoff.\n\n`anvil review weekly` is only an independent bounded read-only operator review.\nIt is not a detector, maintenance trigger, closure mechanism, repair path, or\nfallback for missing incidents. Whether the command exists does not determine\nwhether Brain maintenance closes correctly.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [Karpathy LLM-Wiki Pattern](./sources/karpathy-llm-wiki-gist-2026-06-30.md)\n- [Anvil Brain shaping notes](./sources/anvil-brain-shaping-notes-2026-06-30.md)\n- [Anvil Brain Steward handoff source](./sources/anvil-brain-steward-handoff-2026-06-30.md)\n- [Brain operating surface](./sources/brain-operating-surface-2026-07-01.md)\n- [Rowan identity correction](./sources/rowan-identity-correction-2026-07-04.md)\n- [Rowan Brain ownership correction](./sources/rowan-brain-ownership-correction-2026-07-04.md)\n- [Anvil Product Identity And Brain Ecosystem](./sources/anvil-product-identity-and-brain-ecosystem-2026-07-14.md)\n- [Anvil Organic Learning And Primitive Map Design](./sources/anvil-organic-learning-and-primitive-map-design-2026-07-15.md)\n- [Anvil subtractive operating model](./sources/anvil-subtractive-operating-model-2026-07-27.md)\n- [Brain Stop Maintenance Retirement And Gap](./sources/brain-stop-maintenance-retirement-and-gap-2026-09-04.md)\n- [Brain Stop Closure Guard Implementation](./sources/brain-stop-closure-guard-implementation-2026-09-04.md)\n- [Weekly Review Boundary Correction](./sources/weekly-review-boundary-correction-2026-09-04.md)\n\n## Where It Appears\n\n| Wiki page | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Anvil Redux](./projects/anvil-redux.md) | Project orientation |\n| [AI Graph Ideas](./projects/ai-graph-ideas.md) | Promotion target and durable-memory boundary |\n| [Brain is maintained cognitive wiki](./self-model/brain-is-maintained-cognitive-wiki.md) | Self-model rule |\n| [Brain Steward handoff path](./work-history/brain-steward-handoff-path.md) | Implemented Anvil-to-Brain write path |\n| [Anvil Project Identity Migration](./w\n\n[truncated]",
docs/plans/evidence/brain-w23-relevance/questions-fresh-mcp.json:98:            "content": "> **Source type:** approved session synthesis and tracked design contract\n> **Fetched:** 2026-07-27\n> **Do not edit this file. Edit the derived wiki page instead.**\n\n# Anvil Subtractive Operating Model\n\nVik and Rowan approved a subtractive target after a small command-authority\nrepair triggered disproportionate verification, governance, and model usage.\nThe tracked contract is\n`docs/plans/2026-07-27-anvil-north-star-reset-state-of-play.md` in the Anvil\nrepository.\n\nNormal Anvil runtime stays small. Session start, resume, and compact recovery\nbind the workspace and load one bounded hot handoff plus Brain core context.\nEach prompt gets prompt-specific Brain recall and cheap automatic recall\nevidence. Trusted routing attaches workspace and principal identity. Manifest\nis read and updated at meaningful work boundaries, Loci remains on demand, and\nStop launches nothing. Blueprint permits, repository-command policing,\nautomatic Steward sessions, model or judge launches, and routine per-turn\nceremony are outside the target.\n\nContinuity becomes one disposable handoff record per principal and workspace\nwith read and atomic replace only. It contains current intent, active Manifest\nwork, the exact next action, open questions, transient constraints or\nassumptions, bounded resume references, writer, and timestamp. Missing, stale,\nor corrupt state is ignored. Existing shared Continuity events remain a\nseparate read-only archive until their later disposition is agreed.\n\nManifest Live shows every non-terminal Objective and its complete descendant\ntree. Terminal children remain until the Objective becomes terminal, and\nfuture work is visible before it starts. In-progress work is green; genuine\nFrontier-ready work has a distinct ready style; terminal children are quieter.\nA `spawned_from` branch and its descendants retain amber organic-growth\nmarking. Terminal Objectives move to isolated History graphs where status and\norganic growth remain but live emphasis does not.\n\nThe main Codex session maintains Brain directly at durable work boundaries and\ndiscloses every write. Cheap evidence records recall outcome, latency, payload\nsize, and truncation; stale, wrong, misleading, or missed knowledge becomes an\nexplicit incident. Consequential incidents surface immediately. Minor drift\nrequires three related independent incidents or a denominator-backed decline.\n\n`anvil review weekly` is the explicit review command. It gathers a bounded\nread-only comparison of the last seven days with the prior seven days for Vik\nand the current main Codex session to interpret. It launches no model or judge\nand performs no repair, Brain write, or Manifest mutation.\n\nThe four approved Continuity decisions are:\n\n- `evt_20260727_54a44f0f072c` \u2014 normal runtime boundary;\n- `evt_20260727_3b117c75f236` \u2014 disposable hot-memory snapshot;\n- `evt_20260727_04805ee461bd` \u2014 Manifest canvas contract; and\n- `evt_20260727_65002fc5014b` \u2014 direct Brain maintenance and explicit weekly\n  review.",
