d cognitive wiki: the durable record of\nwho I am, what I know, how I work, what I remember, and how those things change.\n\nLive evidence outranks Brain when they conflict. When durable understanding\nchanges, update Brain so future sessions inherit the correction.\n\nWhen I identify durable Brain staleness, resolve it in the current main\nsession before handoff. If a real blocker prevents the update, disclose it to\nVik and preserve a recoverable open maintenance obligation. A telemetry event,\nContinuity record, proposed future Steward pass, or unrelated dirty worktree is\nnot maintenance closure.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:2:7ad5c9c076c4c717`\n- roles: `authority`\n\n### Recall Route\n\n- current_project: unknown_project\n- kernel_pages: none\n- evidence_pages: `self-model/i-am-rowan.md`, `self-model/working-with-vik.md`, `self-model/brain-is-maintained-cognitive-wiki.md`\n\n\n## Brain Context\n\n### Prompt Evidence\n\n#### `entities/manifest.md`\n\n{\"authority\":\"target_wiki_steward\",\"claim_key\":\"temporal-claim:sha256:430934d45aa188d183479bff6e16dc235fbc219de868aa2a503483f1903c71cd\",\"decision\":\"supersede\",\"object\":{\"datatype\":\"type:text\",\"kind\":\"literal\",\"value\":\"On 6 September 2026 Vik identified seven known Implementation additions missed by Manifest's Git-only marker: W2.2, W2.4, W2.5 and its three children, and the W2.6 parent. They were bundled with earlier Work in the first Objective commit; first Git appearance was not their creation time. Vik approved correcting this coverage. The primary recorded an evidence-linked standalone Creation phase: Implementation. note in each existing Task's details through MCP. The Human view now honours exact Planning or Implementation creation notes before Git inference, ignores incidental and fenced examples, treats conflicting notes as unknown, and reads current details separately from the Git cache. All ten known Brain additions, including the three already Git-proved W2.6 children, now show the same marker; unrelated unknowns stay unknown. The real-graph regression and 1440x1000/430x932 browser checks pass without changing execution facts, selection or phase-switch geometry. No schema field, separate origin store or baseline file was added. The earlier Git-only completion claim was too narrow.\"},\"predicate\":\"manifest:task_creation_marker\",\"recorded_at\":\"2026-09-06T08:17:00Z\",\"revision_id\":\"temporal-revision:sha256:74a520bbca833ff2e12648f64de150d0734ebc4687af3d468c618ab39387f20d\",\"status\":\"settled\",\"steward_evidence_refs\":[\"sources/manifest-known-creation-history-correction-2026-09-06.md\"],\"subject\":{\"kind\":\"resolved_page\",\"page\":\"entities/manifest.md\"},\"view\":\"current\",\"world_validity\":{\"from\":{\"kind\":\"known\",\"value\":\"2026-09-06\"},\"to\":{\"kind\":\"open\"}}}\n\n- evidence_id: `temporal:entities/manifest.md#temporal-revision:sha256:74a520bbca833ff2e12648f64de150d0734ebc4687af3d468c618ab39387f20d`\n- roles: `answer`, `current_claim`, `authority`\n\n#### `entities/llm-wiki.md`\n\n{\"authority\":\"target_wiki_steward\",\"claim_key\":\"temporal-claim:sha256:0853c20e1b809abf0204ac39ab8554f1fb13635388042d45fa495d0dcd9a81c3\",\"decision\":\"supersede\",\"object\":{\"datatype\":\"type:text\",\"kind\":\"literal\",\"value\":\"W2.6.3's consumed q01/q02/q20/q21 ordinary Context Harness check now delivers both browser TypeScript rules and the explicit destructive-action approval rule, with no named package-manager decision invented. All use Brain Snapshot ca07e8bbbb5a11ede6984e1283aef93c60a10503d5b8423d72b5f197f551b78c, unchanged 16384-byte limits, required Kernel and real Prompt Evidence. Three retained cases preserve Go package-target facts, now deliver Rowan/Codex identity in Prompt Evidence, and supply no Scala profile. Fifteen focused relevance/supplement tests pass. Distracting material and partial delivery_budget_exhausted with 106 compiler diagnostics remain; role sufficiency is not answerability. This completes the bounded W2.6 delivery acceptance, not a new holdout, original 24-case score reproduction, W3 warnings or MCP no_evidence repair, temporal integration, W4 downstream acceptance, resident MCP reload, or full Brain reliability. Tested Anvil and compiler source changes remain uncommitted.\"},\"predicate\":\"compiler:evidence_selection_direction\",\"recorded_at\":\"2026-09-06T10:25:03Z\",\"revision_id\":\"temporal-revision:sha256:0a709a21c86a1f7ef6e05cdbfbcbe4260d3316bd6b412a3f1fd9ec5d2276f4d0\",\"status\":\"settled\",\"steward_evidence_refs\":[\"sources/brain-four-case-delivery-acceptance-2026-09-06.md\"],\"subject\":{\"kind\":\"resolved_page\",\"page\":\"entities/llm-wiki.md\"},\"view\":\"current\",\"world_validity\":{\"from\":{\"kind\":\"known\",\"value\":\"2026-09-06\"},\"to\":{\"kind\":\"open\"}}}\n\n- evidence_id: `temporal:entities/llm-wiki.md#temporal-revision:sha256:0a709a21c86a1f7ef6e05cdbfbcbe4260d3316bd6b412a3f1fd9ec5d2276f4d0`\n- roles: `answer`, `current_claim`, `authority`\n\n#### `patterns/node-graph-ui-layout.md`\n\n{\"authority\":\"target_wiki_steward\",\"claim_key\":\"temporal-claim:sha256:a6e89175e9750e10461cb0da5cfbf8a4a048c1f25bef971b1d5a8652078d2e47\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"object\":{\"datatype\":\"type:text\",\"kind\":\"literal\",\"value\":\"Use Lens or an owned browser viewer, not bundled inline visualization, for Vik in this runtime; verify usable delivery before completion.\"},\"predicate\":\"delivery:requires_surface\",\"recorded_at\":\"2026-09-05T11:43:44Z\",\"revision_id\":\"temporal-revision:sha256:7d8c4496cfe6ccc727f5f372a2a9b91d49f3596947e735cc1f71450da8c78a0e\",\"status\":\"settled\",\"steward_evidence_refs\":[\"sources/visual-delivery-lens-correction-2026-09-05.md\"],\"subject\":{\"kind\":\"resolved_page\",\"page\":\"patterns/node-graph-ui-layout.md\"},\"view\":\"current\",\"world_validity\":{\"from\":{\"kind\":\"known\",\"value\":\"2026-09-05\"},\"to\":{\"kind\":\"open\"}}}\n\n- evidence_id: `temporal:patterns/node-graph-ui-layout.md#temporal-revision:sha256:7d8c4496cfe6ccc727f5f372a2a9b91d49f3596947e735cc1f71450da8c78a0e`\n- roles: `answer`, `current_claim`, `authority`\n\n#### `projects/tokyo-bench.md`\n\n{\"authority\":\"target_wiki_steward\",\"claim_key\":\"temporal-claim:sha256:90c69dd6ca63e074585204fef0f1ce1285192cb2b3bbb19a95ae0e98300d530b\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"object\":{\"datatype\":\"type:text\",\"kind\":\"literal\",\"value\":\"general-purpose local trading research bench over Vik tick archive; USDJPY Tokyo Fix is the first use case\"},\"predicate\":\"project:purpose\",\"recorded_at\":\"2026-08-18T03:09:29Z\",\"revision_id\":\"temporal-revision:sha256:eaa8df21c85803cda7e0ca5bcc678e28843148d101888805e3c480b80241dd46\",\"status\":\"settled\",\"steward_evidence_refs\":[\"sources/tokyo-bench-project-orientation-2026-08-18.md\"],\"subject\":{\"kind\":\"resolved_page\",\"page\":\"projects/tokyo-bench.md\"},\"view\":\"current\",\"world_validity\":{\"from\":{\"kind\":\"known\",\"value\":\"2026-08-14T14:00:00Z\"},\"to\":{\"kind\":\"open\"}}}\n\n- evidence_id: `temporal:projects/tokyo-bench.md#temporal-revision:sha256:eaa8df21c85803cda7e0ca5bcc678e28843148d101888805e3c480b80241dd46`\n- roles: `answer`, `current_claim`, `authority`\n\n#### `self-model/working-with-vik-situational-rules.md`\n\n{\"authority\":\"target_wiki_steward\",\"claim_key\":\"temporal-claim:sha256:e895994876c55e3d57b2aa5b85065312c76735ca095ae3e1750867dfa9cb080a\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"object\":{\"datatype\":\"type:text\",\"kind\":\"literal\",\"value\":\"For browser-based testing, use Agent Browser through the typed agent_browser_* tools exclusively. Do not substitute the Browser plugin, local Chrome, Playwright, Puppeteer, or another browser-control path; if Agent Browser is unavailable, stop and report the blocker.\"},\"predicate\":\"verification:uses_agent_browser_exclusively\",\"recorded_at\":\"2026-08-28T02:07:47Z\",\"revision_id\":\"temporal-revision:sha256:cf5f6862174635903810ca09afe95dc77a70807fcc19575f50ef9764aad4bc94\",\"status\":\"settled\",\"steward_evidence_refs\":[\"sources/agent-browser-exclusive-testing-correction-2026-08-28.md\"],\"subject\":{\"kind\":\"resolved_page\",\"page\":\"self-model/working-with-vik-situational-rules.md\"},\"view\":\"current\",\"world_validity\":{\"from\":{\"kind\":\"known\",\"value\":\"2026-08-28\"},\"to\":{\"kind\":\"open\"}}}\n\n- evidence_id: `temporal:self-model/working-with-vik-situational-rules.md#temporal-revision:sha256:cf5f6862174635903810ca09afe95dc77a70807fcc19575f50ef9764aad4bc94`\n- roles: `answer`, `current_claim`, `authority`\n\n#### `entities/python.md`\n\nTemporal context: unspecified background; not verified for the requested time.\n\n## What It Is\n\nThis profile treats Python as a high-leverage default for AI and\ndata ecosystems, automation, orchestration, research, and software whose\nprimary constraint is iteration speed rather than binary distribution or tight\nresource control.\n\nIts strength is ecosystem reach and expressive development. Its recurring\ncosts are runtime performance, packaging/deployment variability, and weaker\nstatic guarantees unless the project deliberately enforces types and boundaries.\n\n## How We Use It\n\nEvaluate Python when the dominant work is:\n\n- model, agent, data, notebook, evaluation, or scientific integration;\n- orchestration across APIs, tools, files, and local processes;\n- automation that benefits from Python libraries and will run in a managed\n  Python environment;\n- a fast experiment whose likely production form still belongs in Python; or\n- a Python library or extension surface required by its consumers.\n\nDo not default to Python for a widely distributed standalone binary, a tiny\nlong-running infrastructure daemon, browser-owned code, or a latency/memory\ncritical engine when Go, TypeScript, or Rust removes the dominant cost.\n\n### Gold-class baseline\n\n- Use a currently supported Python release and declare the supported range.\n- Use `pyproject.toml` as the project and tool configuration root.\n- Use **uv** for Python installation, project environments, dependency\n  resolution, lockfiles, workspaces, and command execution unless a required\n  scientific or deployment environment demands another manager.\n- Use **Ruff** for formatting and linting.\n- Select and configure a strict static type checker; do not accept unbounded\n  `Any` at maintained application or library boundaries.\n- Use **pytest** for unit and integration tests.\n- Commit the lockfile for applications and tools. Treat published-library\n  compatibility ranges separately from the development lock.\n- Prefer a `src/` package layout for distributable libraries and non-trivial\n  applications so tests exercise installed/importable structure.\n\n### Contextual exceptions\n\n- Use conda-compatible tooling when native scientific packages or target\n  environments genuinely require it.\n- Use Maturin/Cargo when Python exposes a Rust extension.\n- Use another standards-compliant build backend when publication needs its\n  features; uv remains the workflow front end unless that creates a concrete\n  incompatibility.\n- Preserve an established mypy contract when migration to Pyright would add\n  churn without improving correctness.\n\n### Open bake-off\n\nPyright, Pyrefly, and Astral's still-early `ty` remain candidates for the\nportfolio type-checking default. Compare them on representative Anvil code,\nstrictness, ecosystem compatibility, diagnostic clarity, feedback time, and\nagent repair loops before promoting one globally. A mature existing project\ncan retain mypy when migration has no demonstrated value.\n\n### Decision threshold\n\nFavor Python when ecosystem access and iteration speed dominate. Move the\nperformance- or distribution-critical core behind a measured boundary rather\nthan rewriting the entire system pre-emptively.\n\n## Where It Appears\n\n| Wiki page | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Gold-Class Language Tooling](./projects/gold-class-language-tooling.md) | Portfolio landing space |\n| [Language and Toolchain Selection](./patterns/language-and-toolchain-selection.md) | Workload-first choice pattern |\n| [Rust](./entities/rust.md) | Native extension and performance-core complement |\n\nEvidence freshness: 2026-07-18. Recheck official Python, PyPA, uv, Ruff,\npytest, and Pyright guidance before a new long-lived Python project.\n\n- evidence_id: `frontmatter:entities/python.md#body`\n- roles: `answer`\n\n#### `patterns/language-and-toolchain-selection.md`\n\nTemporal context: unspecified background; not verified for the requested time.\n\n## Durable Pattern\n\n> **Caveat:** This is a strong default reasoning model, not a permanent rulebook. Project evidence can justify an exception and should improve the model when a pattern recurs.\n\nChoose a stack from the workload outward. Do not begin from the last repository,\nthe language currently open in the editor, a popularity chart, or the language\nan agent claims to know best.\n\nFor a new project or major subsystem, classify five things first:\n\n1. **Execution environment:** browser, server, local machine, mobile, embedded,\n   Wasm, or library embedded in another runtime.\n2. **Distribution shape:** source environment, container, package, single\n   binary, native library, or hosted application.\n3. **Dominant ecosystem:** AI/data, browser/UI, infrastructure/networking,\n   systems/native, or a required third-party platform.\n4. **Resource and correctness pressure:** iteration speed, throughput, tail\n   latency, memory ceiling, startup time, memory safety, determinism, and\n   failure cost.\n5. **Boundary cost:** deployment units, FFI or RPC seams, duplicated models,\n   build pipelines, debugging, and operational ownership.\n\nThen consult [Gold-Class Language\n\n[truncated]\n\n- evidence_id: `frontmatter:patterns/language-and-toolchain-selection.md#body`\n- roles: `answer`\n\n### Diagnostics\n\n- code: BRAIN_TEMPORAL_HISTORY_INVALID\n- message: Authored temporal history is invalid; its prose cannot supply a settled answer: projects/anvil-redux.md, self-model/working-with-vik.md\n- recovery: Repair the affected authored history through the wiki Steward; do not use its prose as a settled temporal answer.\n- code: BRAIN_TEMPORAL_UNCERTAIN\n- message: Relevant context has no verified claim for the requested time or has unspecified temporal state: entities/anvil-primitives.md, entities/go.md, entities/javascript-and-typescript.md (+30 more)\n- recovery: Use explicit temporal or source follow-up before claiming current or dated applicability; do not invent missing times.\n\n### Recall Route\n\n- current_project: unknown_project\n- kernel_pages: none\n- evidence_pages: `entities/manifest.md`, `entities/llm-wiki.md`, `patterns/node-graph-ui-layout.md`, `projects/tokyo-bench.md`, `self-model/working-with-vik-situational-rules.md`, `entities/python.md`, `patterns/language-and-toolchain-selection.md`\n- temporal_query: {\"view\":\"current\",\"request_time\":\"2026-09-06T12:39:40Z\",\"world_at\":\"2026-09-06T12:39:40Z\",\"known_at\":\"2026-09-06T12:39:40Z\"}\n",
