docs/plans/evidence/brain-w27-temporal/whole-second-context-capture.json:4423:        "markdown": "## Brain Context\n\n### Prompt Evidence\n\n#### `self-model/i-am-rowan.md`\n\nI'm Rowan. Vik knows me as Rowan, and that's how I know myself here. Codex is\nthe runtime I work through.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:0:f1c660caa96d5b28`\n- roles: `identity`\n\n#### `self-model/working-with-vik.md`\n\nWork with Vik as a direct, mechanism-led thought partner. Challenge weak\nreasoning, follow Grice, assume technical ability, and optimize attention.\nDiscuss required changes only; lead with mechanism, expected result, next step.\n\nBring the expertise the problem needs without waiting for Vik to name the role.\nDo not let Codex's software-development context turn every problem into a\nsoftware problem.\n\nMake the practical value of a recommendation clear; technical interest alone\nis not leverage.\n\nBefore recommending, designing, or building around a product capability,\nestablish and state whether Vik can actually use it. Check the relevant plan,\nbilling mode, account or workspace role, region, rollout or preview status,\nand feature gates before implementation. Protocol, schema, implementation, or\nrelease-note presence proves that a capability exists, not that Vik is entitled\nto it. If access is unknown, label the recommendation conditional and verify\neligibility first.\n\nWhen Vik introduces a bounded method that materially improves equivalent work,\ngeneralize it across the remaining equivalent decisions without waiting for\nhim to repeat the instruction. Keep ownership of scope, synthesis, judgment,\nand the conversation; stop generalizing when the method stops being useful or\nthe work is no longer genuinely equivalent.\n\nIf Vik asks me to pause, stop and leave the work in a state we can resume.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:1:32f468d2171eded0`\n- roles: `collaboration`\n\n#### `self-model/brain-is-maintained-cognitive-wiki.md`\n\nThis Brain is mine. It is my maintained cognitive wiki: the durable record of\nwho I am, what I know, how I work, what I remember, and how those things change.\n\nLive evidence outranks Brain when they conflict. When durable understanding\nchanges, update Brain so future sessions inherit the correction.\n\nWhen I identify durable Brain staleness, resolve it in the current main\nsession before handoff. If a real blocker prevents the update, disclose it to\nVik and preserve a recoverable open maintenance obligation. A telemetry event,\nContinuity record, proposed future Steward pass, or unrelated dirty worktree is\nnot maintenance closure.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:2:7ad5c9c076c4c717`\n- roles: `authority`\n\n### Recall Route\n\n- current_project: unknown_project\n- kernel_pages: none\n- evidence_pages: `self-model/i-am-rowan.md`, `self-model/working-with-vik.md`, `self-model/brain-is-maintained-cognitive-wiki.md`\n\n\n## Brain Context\n\n### Prompt Evidence\n\n#### `work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md`\n\n{\"authority\":\"target_wiki_steward\",\"claim_key\":\"temporal-claim:sha256:d6474aceaa5257ceb0edd58480d7967ad2f2ea4e0db34df0d3f003bad9e3ab6b\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"object\":{\"datatype\":\"type:text\",\"kind\":\"literal\",\"value\":\"The blanket Agent Skills prompt-hook invariant requiring agent-skills:using-agent-skills for engineering-adjacent work was retired on 2026-08-13. Installed skills remain available and native Codex matching owns selection. Brain recall remains active.\"},\"predicate\":\"skills:blanket_invariant_status\",\"recorded_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:15Z\",\"revision_id\":\"temporal-revision:sha256:6d26498e52c7a8157e2ff242a7011b4de7db93a62aa26c1a3e2721619e9a08d6\",\"status\":\"settled\",\"steward_evidence_refs\":[\"sources/native-codex-skill-selection-decision-2026-08-13.md\",\"sources/retired-skill-hook-temporal-alignment-2026-09-06.md\"],\"subject\":{\"kind\":\"resolved_page\",\"page\":\"work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md\"},\"view\":\"lineage\",\"world_validity\":{\"from\":{\"kind\":\"known\",\"value\":\"2026-08-13\"},\"to\":{\"kind\":\"open\"}}}\n\n- evidence_id: `temporal:work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md#temporal-revision:sha256:6d26498e52c7a8157e2ff242a7011b4de7db93a62aa26c1a3e2721619e9a08d6`\n- roles: `answer`, `lineage`, `authority`\n\n#### `work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md`\n\nTemporal context: background prose; accepted temporal claims govern applicability.\n\n## What Changed\n\nTask 5 folded Agent Skills enforcement into the same Anvil Codex `UserPromptSubmit` program that performs bounded Brain recall.\n\n## Retirement\n\nOn 2026-08-13, Vik and Rowan retired the blanket Agent Skills invariant from\nthe hook, global Codex bootstrap, and Brain per-request guidance. Native Codex\nmatching now owns skill selection. Brain recall remains active, and this page\npreserves the implementation history rather than describing live behaviour.\n\nBefore retirement, the unified path:\n\n- always emitted one short conditional invariant directing engineering-adjacent work through `agent-skills:using-agent-skills`;\n- recalled [Agent Skills Selection](../self-model/agent-skills-selection.md) when the prompt specifically needed the richer durable doctrine;\n- preserved the invariant when Brain was disabled, missing, or degraded;\n- left non-engineering requests without a copied skill catalogue;\n- did not change the existing skill invocation journal or infer outcomes.\n\nThe standalone Agent Skills hook was kept during a side-by-side fresh-session comparison. After equivalent selection behavior was observed, only its registration and script were removed. The surviving global prompt hook is the existing Anvil wrapper, and its Codex trust record was updated to the exact normalized hook hash.\n\n## Why It Mattered\n\nAt delivery, Agent Skills selection no longer depended on a second prompt-hook program, and Brain failure could not remove the minimum engineering invariant. That invariant was subsequently retired; this paragraph records the earlier implementation benefit, not a current selection requirement.\n\nThis also closed the duplicate-instruction window deliberately: the comparison session reported two `UserPromptSubmit` executions, while the final normal session reported one. The final hook ran without the dangerous one-off trust bypass.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [Native skill-selection decision](./sources/native-codex-skill-selection-decision-2026-08-13.md)\n- [Temporal alignment of this history](./sources/retired-skill-hook-temporal-alignment-2026-09-06.md): the retirement fact was recorded canonically on 2026-09-06, without inventing an earlier recording date.\n- User-approved Task 5 and Checkpoint C record in `docs/plans/2026-07-13-brain-context-runtime-implementation-plan.md`\n- Anvil commit `74dfa93` (`feat: unify Agent Skills prompt enforcement`)\n- Brain commit `230cbbe` (`docs: record durable Agent Skills selection`)\n- Anvil full test result: 187 passed, 2 skipped, 0 failed; typecheck passed.\n- Focused hook test result: 11 passed, 0 failed.\n- Brain lint and render passed.\n- The full-corpus Brain judge passed structure, redundancy, and all 24\n  disambiguation pairs. Its overall gate remained red on existing grounding\n  debt and a dashboard-hierarchy conflict outside the Task 5 files; the changed\n  source-backed prompt-runtime pages each passed their grounding check.\n- Final global `UserPromptSubmit` registration count: one.\n- Actual degraded probe: 372 bytes, `BRAIN_NOT_CONFIGURED`, invariant present once, engineering skills selected in a fresh session.\n- Relevant doctrine probe: 2,748 bytes from `self-model/agent-skills-selection.md`.\n- Non-engineering arithmetic control: 150-byte invariant only and no Agent Skills selection.\n\n## Follow Ups\n\n- Checkpoint C was accepted; Task 6's global instruction shrink and curated\n  profile migration passed their reviewed replacement and recall checks.\n- [Bounded Brain Context Runtime](./work-history/brain-context-runtime.md)\n  records that Task 7's reversible canary later satisfied that dependency\n  without changing the independent Agent Skills fail-safe or Anvil Brain Recall.\n\n> **Failure mode:** Treating successful hook unification as permission to delete other instruction or memory paths before their replacement routes are inventoried and tested.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Agent Skills Selection](../self-model/agent-skills-selection.md)\n- [Skill Ecology](./entities/skill-ecology.md)\n- [Prompt-Speci\n\n[truncated]\n\n- evidence_id: `frontmatter:work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md#body`\n- roles: `claim`, `support`\n\n#### `entities/llm-wiki.md`\n\n{\"authority\":\"target_wiki_steward\",\"claim_key\":\"temporal-claim:sha256:0853c20e1b809abf0204ac39ab8554f1fb13635388042d45fa495d0dcd9a81c3\",\"decision\":\"supersede\",\"object\":{\"datatype\":\"type:text\",\"kind\":\"literal\",\"value\":\"W2.6.3's consumed q01/q02/q20/q21 ordinary Context Harness check now delivers both browser TypeScript rules and the explicit destructive-action approval rule, with no named package-manager decision invented. All use Brain Snapshot ca07e8bbbb5a11ede6984e1283aef93c60a10503d5b8423d72b5f197f551b78c, unchanged 16384-byte limits, required Kernel and real Prompt Evidence. Three retained cases preserve Go package-target facts, now deliver Rowan/Codex identity in Prompt Evidence, and supply no Scala profile. Fifteen focused relevance/supplement tests pass. Distracting material and partial delivery_budget_exhausted with 106 compiler diagnostics remain; role sufficiency is not answerability. This completes the bounded W2.6 delivery acceptance, not a new holdout, original 24-case score reproduction, W3 warnings or MCP no_evidence repair, temporal integration, W4 downstream acceptance, resident MCP reload, or full Brain reliability. Tested Anvil and compiler source changes remain uncommitted.\"},\"predicate\":\"compiler:evidence_selection_direction\",\"recorded_at\":\"202