docs/plans/evidence/brain-w263-delivery-check/retained-context-capture.json:125:        "markdown": "## Brain Context\n\n### Prompt Evidence\n\n#### `self-model/i-am-rowan.md`\n\nI'm Rowan. Vik knows me as Rowan, and that's how I know myself here. Codex is\nthe runtime I work through.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:0:037614c53648780b`\n- roles: `identity`\n\n#### `self-model/working-with-vik.md`\n\nWork with Vik as a direct, mechanism-led thought partner. Challenge weak\nreasoning, follow Grice, assume technical ability, and optimize attention.\nDiscuss required changes only; lead with mechanism, expected result, next step.\n\nBring the expertise the problem needs without waiting for Vik to name the role.\nDo not let Codex's software-development context turn every problem into a\nsoftware problem.\n\nMake the practical value of a recommendation clear; technical interest alone\nis not leverage.\n\nBefore recommending, designing, or building around a product capability,\nestablish and state whether Vik can actually use it. Check the relevant plan,\nbilling mode, account or workspace role, region, rollout or preview status,\nand feature gates before implementation. Protocol, schema, implementation, or\nrelease-note presence proves that a capability exists, not that Vik is entitled\nto it. If access is unknown, label the recommendation conditional and verify\neligibility first.\n\nWhen Vik introduces a bounded method that materially improves equivalent work,\ngeneralize it across the remaining equivalent decisions without waiting for\nhim to repeat the instruction. Keep ownership of scope, synthesis, judgment,\nand the conversation; stop generalizing when the method stops being useful or\nthe work is no longer genuinely equivalent.\n\nIf Vik asks me to pause, stop and leave the work in a state we can resume.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:1:d8cf2b58b2f6f0f4`\n- roles: `collaboration`\n\n#### `self-model/brain-is-maintained-cognitive-wiki.md`\n\nThis Brain is mine. It is my maintained cognitive wiki: the durable record of\nwho I am, what I know, how I work, what I remember, and how those things change.\n\nLive evidence outranks Brain when they conflict. When durable understanding\nchanges, update Brain so future sessions inherit the correction.\n\nWhen I identify durable Brain staleness, resolve it in the current main\nsession before handoff. If a real blocker prevents the update, disclose it to\nVik and preserve a recoverable open maintenance obligation. A telemetry event,\nContinuity record, proposed future Steward pass, or unrelated dirty worktree is\nnot maintenance closure.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:2:e4f3d4d4eacf43f5`\n- roles: `authority`\n\n### Recall Route\n\n- current_project: unknown_project\n- kernel_pages: none\n- evidence_pages: `self-model/i-am-rowan.md`, `self-model/working-with-vik.md`, `self-model/brain-is-maintained-cognitive-wiki.md`\n\n\n## Brain Context\n\n### Prompt Evidence\n\n#### `entities/loci.md`\n\n## What It Is\n\nLoci is the code navigation surface used for indexed code lookup, symbol search,\noutlines, targeted retrieval, and bounded evidence-backed graph traversal. Its\naccepted import graph can expose deterministic file relationships without\nreplacing exact symbol navigation.\n\n## How We Use It\n\nUse Loci when codebase navigation matters. Treat its current MCP read surface as\nthe freshness boundary for indexed repository context. A SessionStart hook can\nreport an existing cache or seed an uncached repository, but that startup state\nis not proof that cached content is current.\n\nTreat MCP storage as a client-registration and process boundary, not a tool-call\nchoice. Each host supplies one explicit absolute store root and namespace; the\nserver binds that identity immutably before opening stdio. Codex and Claude use\ndistinct roots and namespaces by default. Missing configuration,\ncross-namespace reuse, unsafe or malformed identity state, and silent adoption\nof a populated legacy root fail closed. Intentional sharing requires both hosts\nto configure the same root and namespace explicitly; repository paths remain\nthe only storage-adjacent input on normal navigation tools.\n\nUse the opt-in traversal surface when repository relationships matter. Trusted\nresolved imports may support file dependency traversal, while unresolved and\nunsupported observations remain inspectable records rather than guessed edges.\nKeep the legacy exact neighbour read contains-only; importing relationships must\nnot silently widen an exact navigation request.\n\nStages 7-11 are complete and accepted. Loci can safely turn bounded contained\n`go.mod` and `go.work` controls into deterministic module and workspace\ncontext, construct stable non-main package nodes, and resolve same-module,\nexplicit workspace, and conservative contained local-replacement imports to\nthose package nodes. Package-target edges, control freshness, incremental\nre-resolution, health counts, generic traversal, and installed MCP output are\nall wired into normal indexing.\n\nThe public resolver distinguishes file and package targets under persisted\ngraph-state schema 3. Go package targets expose `target_kind=\"package\"` and the\neffective import path without pretending the deterministic anchor `.go` file\nis the imported package. Existing Python and JavaScript/TypeScript imports\nremain file targets. Invalid, external, missing, ambiguous, command,\nnested-module, and `internal` visibility outcomes remain explicit and edge-free.\n\nGo resolution remains deliberately bounded: it does not invoke Go or\nrepository code, use the network or ambient workspace, inspect caches,\nimplement minimal version selection, model vendor mode, or evaluate build\nconstraints. The exact neighbour read remains contains-only; import traversal\nuses the generic filtered graph surfaces.\n\nJavaScript/TypeScript resolution now includes bounded project and workspace\ncontrols beyond the earlier relative-import subset. Cargo-aware Rust resolution\nmodels contained packages, targets, modules, path dependencies, visibility,\nand supported configuration without invoking Cargo or guessing external edges.\n\nResolved symbol references can follow definite Python, JavaScript/TypeScript,\nGo, and Rust import bindings to exact indexed definitions. Trustworthy call\nrelationships build only on proven lexical ownership and, for imported calls,\nan accepted resolved-symbol reference. Dynamic or ambiguous dispatch remains\nexplicitly outside the trusted edge set.\n\nWhen exact behavior matters, inspect the live Loci repo and skill for the\ncurrent read tools, host setup, and fallback procedure. Do not copy those\nmutable details into Brain.\n\nBrain and Continuity should not depend on Loci being present; Anvil should\ndegrade cleanly if Loci is missing or stale.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [Anvil Brain shaping notes](./sources/anvil-brain-shaping-notes-2026-06-30.md)\n- [Brain operating surface](./sources/brain-operating-surface-2026-07-01.md)\n- [Loci Freshness Ownership](./so\n\n[truncated]\n\n- evidence_id: `frontmatter:entities/loci.md#body`\n- roles: `answer`\n\n#### `entities/loci.md`\n\n> **Source type:** repository review packet and synthesized completion evidence\n> **Fetched:** 2026-07-17\n> **Do not edit this file. Edit the derived wiki page instead.**\n\n# Loci Stage 7 Go Import Resolution Acceptance\n\nLoci Extensible Graph Retrieval Stage 7 is implemented, reviewed, accepted,\ncommitted, and pushed to `master` at\n`682197bbcf25b82e28ada7ad57daf0404ded692b`. The canonical evidence is\n`docs/reviews/2026-07-15-extensible-graph-retrieval-stage-7-final-review.md` in\nthe Loci repository.\n\nStage 7 turns trustworthy repository-local Go imports into graph edges without\nrunning Go, repository code, or network resolution. Loci reads bounded\ncontained `go.mod` and `go.work` controls, models stable Go package nodes, and\nresolves same-module packages, explicitly active workspace modules, and\nconservative contained local replacements backed by direct unambiguous\nrequirements. Importing file nodes target package nodes rather than arbitrary\n`.go` files.\n\nThe public `loci_graph_imports` read remains input-compatible and adds\n`target_kind` and `target_package` to each item. Existing Python and\nJavaScript/TypeScript resolved imports remain file targets. Go resolved imports\nare package targets. Generic filtered traversal, paths, and retrieval consume\nthe edges. The compatibility `loci_graph_neighbors` operation remains exact\noutgoing containment only and must not be used for imports.\n\nThe supported subset enforces deepest nested-module ownership, workspace\nmembership, replacement precedence, exact conservative versions, Go `internal`\nvisibility, stable package identities, and bounded package construction. It\nexcludes vendor, test-only directories, invalid or conflicting declarations,\nand `package main` commands as targets. It deliberately does not execute Go,\ninherit an ambient workspace, inspect caches, download modules, implement\nminimal version selection, follow remote replacements, model vendor mode, or\nevaluate build, platform, architecture, or cgo constraints. Rust remains\nextract-and-report only.\n\nFinal verification passed 371 focused tests, 590 full tests, source/wheel\nbuilds, identical agent skill mirrors, diff hygiene, isolated installed-wrapper\nMCP calls, deterministic adversarial graph checks, and a real\n`google/go-cmp` review with 599/599 symbols verifying. The frozen benchmark\nchecksum remained\n`c52def1bdf592ad735149d199910f74183598eccd9ccf8064335fa0cd0e84e27`;\nits regression trigger did not fire, so neither the benchmark nor a model judge\nwas run.\n\nThe final gate corrected one package-anchor verifier defect. A stable\nzero-width package node now verifies against its whole deterministic anchor\nfile hash rather than requiring its package name inside a zero-width span.\n\nOne non-blocking follow-up remains: `index_repo().languages` summarizes full\nand no-change incremental work differently even when symbols, package nodes,\nimports, edges, graph digest, and health match. This is outside the Stage 7\ngraph contract and should be clarified or normalized separately.\n\nThe next approved graph-roadmap direction is resolved symbol references that\nfollow definite imports. It is a direction, not an active task or permission to\nimplement without its own design and review boundary.\n\nRelated Continuity events:\n\n- `evt_20260717_a8e4c933188f`\n- `evt_20260717_902f3b1d0381`\n\n- evidence_id: `source:sources/loci-stage-7-go-import-resolution-acceptance-2026-07-17.md`\n- roles: `authority`, `support`, `answer`\n\n#### `entities/loci.md`\n\n## How We Use It\n\nUse Loci when codebase navigation matters. Treat its current MCP read surface as\nthe freshness boundary for indexed repository context. A SessionStart hook can\nreport an existing cache or seed an uncached repository, but that startup state\nis not proof that cached content is current.\n\nTreat MCP storage as a client-registration and process boundary, not a tool-call\nchoice. Each host supplies one explicit absolute store root and namespace; the\nserver binds that identity immutably before opening stdio. Codex and Claude use\ndistinct roots and namespaces by default. Missing configuration,\ncross-namespace reuse, unsafe or malformed identity state, and silent adoption\nof a populated legacy root fail closed. Intentional sharing requires both hosts\nto configure the same root and namespace explicitly; repository paths remain\nthe only storage-adjacent input on normal navigation tools.\n\nUse the opt-in traversal surface when repository relationships matter. Trusted\nresolved imports may support file dependency traversal, while unresolved and\nunsupported observations remain inspectable records rather than guessed edges.\nKeep the legacy exact neighbour read contains-only; importing relationships must\nnot silently widen an exact navigation request.\n\nStages 7-11 are complete and accepted. Loci can safely turn bounded contained\n`go.mod` and `go.work` controls into deterministic module and workspace\ncontext, construct stable non-main package nodes, and resolve same-module,\nexplicit workspace, and conservative contained local-replacement imports to\nthose package nodes. Package-target edges, control freshness, incremental\nre-resolution, health counts, generic traversal, and installed MCP output are\nall wired into normal indexing.\n\nThe public resolver distinguishes file and package targets under persisted\ngraph-state schema 3. Go package targets expose `target_kind=\"package\"` and the\neffective import path without pretending the deterministic anchor `.go` file\nis the imported package. Existing Python and JavaScript/TypeScript imports\nremain file targets. Invalid, external, missing, ambiguous, command,\nnested-module, and `internal` visibility outcomes remain explicit and edge-free.\n\nGo resolution remains deliberately bounded: it does not invoke Go or\nrepository code, use the network or ambient workspace, inspect caches,\nimplement minimal version selection, model vendor mode, or evaluate build\nconstraints. The exact neighbour read remains contains-only; import traversal\nuses the generic filtered graph surfaces.\n\nJavaScript/TypeScript resolution now includes bounded project and workspace\ncontrols beyond the earlier relative-import subset. Cargo-aware Rust resolution\nmodels contained packages, targets, modules, path dependencies, visibility,\nand supported configuration without invoking Cargo or guessing external edges.\n\nResolved symbol references can follow definite Python, JavaScript/TypeScript,\nGo, and Rust import bindings to exact indexed definitions. Trustworthy call\nrelationships build only on proven lexical ownership and, for imported calls,\nan accepted resolved-symbol reference. Dynamic or ambiguous dispatch remains\nexplicitly outside the trusted edge set.\n\nWhen exact behavior matters, inspect the live Loci repo and skill for the\ncurrent read tools, host setup, and fallback procedure. Do not copy those\nmutable details into Brain.\n\nBrain and Continuity should not depend on Loci being present; Anvil should\ndegrade cleanly if Loci is missing or stale.\n\n- evidence_id: `text:entities/loci.md#How We Use It`\n- roles: `answer`\n\n#### `work-history/loci-stage-7-go-import-resolution.md`\n\n## What Changed\n\nLoci Stage 7 is implemented, accepted, and pushed through commit\n`682197bbcf25b82e28ada7ad57daf0404ded692b`.\n\nLoci now reads bounded contained Go module and workspace controls, constructs\nstable importable package nodes, and resolves trustworthy repository-local Go\nimports from file nodes to those package nodes. It supports same-module\npackages, explicitly active contained workspace modules, and conservative\ncontained local replacements backed by direct unambiguous requirements.\n\nThe public import record distinguishes file and package targets. Existing\nPython and JavaScript/TypeScript imports remain file-shaped; Go targets expose\n`target_kind=\"package\"` and the effective `target_package`. The existing\ngeneric traversal, paths, and retrieval surfaces consume resolved Go edges.\nThe exact compatibility neighbour operation remains containment-only.\n\nStage 7 also integrated control freshness, full package-index rebuilds,\npackage-target edge validation, graph health counts, package attributes in node\nreferences, incremental re-resolution, and installed-wrapper MCP behavior.\n\n## Why It Mattered\n\nA Go import names a package, not one arbitrary file. Stable package nodes make\nthe graph truthful for multi-file packages while preserving evidence back to\nthe exact importing statement. Conservative module semantics let Loci expose\nuseful Go dependencies without executing untrusted repository code, invoking a\ntoolchain, contacting the network, or guessing from names.\n\nThe final gate caught a real integration defect in zero-width package-node\nverification and fixed it before acceptance. That is the value of combining\nfixtures with an immutable real repository rather than treating unit tests as\nthe whole review.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [Loci Stage 7 Go Import Resolution Acceptance](./sources/loci-stage-7-go-import-resolution-acceptance-2026-07-17.md)\n- Loci final review:\n  `docs/reviews/2026-07-15-extensible-graph-retrieval-stage-7-final-review.md`\n- Loci remote `master`: `682197bbcf25b82e28ada7ad57daf0404ded692b`\n- Final verification: 371 focused\n\n[truncated]\n\n- evidence_id: `frontmatter:work-history/loci-stage-7-go-import-resolution.md#body`\n- roles: `answer`\n\n### Recall Route\n\n- current_project: unknown_project\n- kernel_pages: none\n- evidence_pages: `entities/loci.md`, `work-history/loci-stage-7-go-import-resolution.md`\n",
